From: =?UTF-8?q?S=C3=A9bastien=20Celles?= <s.celles@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 7 Jun 2026 13:39:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 48/62] verimark: try 35-byte 0x96 03 commit on IT (DT prefix
 shape, no SID)

Status progression of the IT 0x96 03 commit by payload size :
  1B    -> 0x0504  (data missing)
  17B   -> 0x0104  (unknown_op family)
  123B  -> 0x0404  (bad state, full DT layout)

The DT 123-byte layout places the TUID at offset 18 preceded by
a length marker 0x10 (=16) at offset 14. Hypothesis : the IT
firmware reads the prefix the same way but expects no SID
payload and no footer. Build [0x03][zeros 1..13][0x10 @ 14]
[zeros 15..17][TUID @ 18..33][0x01 @ 34], total 35 bytes.
---
 libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c | 23 ++++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
index dd6367d..7469328 100644
--- a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
@@ -2583,16 +2583,21 @@ enroll_sm_run_state(FpiSsm *ssm, FpDevice *dev)
         const gboolean is_it = (usb != NULL &&
                                 g_usb_device_get_pid(usb) == VERIMARK_PID_IT);
         if (is_it) {
-            /* 1-byte payload gave 0x0504 (vs 0x0404 from DT 123-byte) —
-             * progress, but still rejected. Next hypothesis : the IT
-             * commit just needs sub-cmd + TUID, no SID footer. Build
-             * [0x03][TUID 16B] = 17 bytes. */
-            uint8_t it_commit_payload[17];
-            it_commit_payload[0] = 0x03;
-            memcpy(it_commit_payload + 1, ctx->new_tuid,
+            /* Status progression : 1B -> 0x0504, 17B -> 0x0104,
+             * 123B (DT) -> 0x0404. The TUID position in the payload
+             * matters. The DT lays out [0x03][...zeros...][0x10 @ 14]
+             * [...zeros...][TUID @ 18][0x01 @ 34]... — TUID is preceded
+             * by a length marker (0x10 = 16). Try mirroring that
+             * prefix exactly through byte 34, dropping the SID/footer.
+             * 35 bytes total. */
+            uint8_t it_commit_payload[35] = {0};
+            it_commit_payload[0]  = 0x03;          /* sub-cmd commit */
+            it_commit_payload[14] = 0x10;          /* TUID length = 16 */
+            memcpy(it_commit_payload + 18, ctx->new_tuid,
                    VERIMARK_STORAGE_TUID_LEN);
-            fp_warn("verimark: IT enroll sending 0x96 03 with 17-byte payload "
-                    "(sub-cmd + 16B TUID)");
+            it_commit_payload[34] = 0x01;          /* DT marker */
+            fp_warn("verimark: IT enroll sending 0x96 03 with 35-byte payload "
+                    "(DT prefix shape, no SID/footer)");
             verimark_session_call_opcode_async(&self->session, self->transport,
                 3000, 0x96, it_commit_payload, sizeof(it_commit_payload),
                 cancel, enr_cb_commit, ssm);
